{
  "description": "People and messages (protocol/14-people-and-messages.md; NIP-02 and NIP-17). `follows`: `list` is the follow list a change starts from (`followList`, or null where none was found), `change` is what was asked, `expect` is the list to be signed, or null where nothing is signed, and `follows` is who it names. `fromAWorld`: what a signer does when a world it was let asks for one change (`followForWorld`): `list` is what the world handed over, `seen` the time of the newest list the signer has seen, and `expect` the list it signs for the first key, or null where it refuses. `messages`: `wrap` is a kind 1059 event and `reader` names the test key that tries to open it; `expect` is the message, or null where a reader must drop it. The wraps here are signed by a fixed throwaway key with fixed nonces so that they are reproducible: a real one uses a new key each time.",
